      "title": "Laboratory Technician",
      "description": "Career Opportunities: Laboratory Technician (23001) JavaScript is turned off in your web browser. Turn it on to take full advantage of this site, then refresh the page. Loading... Skip to Main Content Career Opportunities: Laboratory Technician (23001) Requisition ID 23001 - Posted - Type of position (2) - Area of Activity (1) - Rate of Participation (1) - Faculty / Service (1) - Personnel Category (1)  Job Description Print Preview Apply Save Job Email Job to Friend Return to List Introduction UNIL is a leading international teaching and research institution, with over 5,000 employees and 17,000 students split between its Dorigny campus, CHUV and Epalinges. As an employer, UNIL encourages excellence, individual recognition and responsibility. unil.ch/work Presentation The mission of the SOxHiF Core Facility is to provide users with shared access to advanced technologies in histology, multiplex imaging, and spatial and multi-omics analyses, as well as scientific and technical support for the design and implementation of complex experiments. Its activities include data generation using established protocols, the optimization of technical procedures, and contributing to the development and validation of new methods, in line with technological advances and evolving user needs. Within this framework, the Laboratory Technician will be responsible for independently preparing, processing, and analyzing biological samples using advanced histology, immunohistochemistry, multiplex immunofluorescence, in situ hybridization, transcriptomics, and imaging techniques. The Laboratory Technician will also contribute to ensuring the quality, traceability, and reproducibility of analyses, as well as to the optimization of protocols and the proper functioning of the facility's equipment. Job information Expected start date in position: As soon as possible, or by mutual agreement Contract length: One-year contract, renewable Activity rate: 100% Workplace: Epalinges (Biopôle) Your responsibilities Develop and perform histology, immunohistochemistry, multiplex immunofluorescence and spatial transcriptomics workflows. Prepare, process and analyze biological samples for research projects. Ensure high standards of quality, traceability and reproducibility. Support instrument maintenance and troubleshooting activities. Manage laboratory consumables and reagents. Train and support platform users in the application of advanced technologies. Contribute to the implementation and development of innovative workflows and services. Your qualifications Diploma ES in Life Sciences, Biology or a related field. Hands-on experience in histology and immunohistochemistry. Strong interest in multiplex imaging and spatial transcriptomics technologies. Experience in molecular biology is an asset. Autonomous, organized and detail-oriented working style. Strong communication skills and ability to work in a multidisciplinary environment. Interest in cutting-edge technologies and innovation in life sciences. What the position offers you We offer a nice working place in a multicultural, diverse and dynamic academic environment. Opportunities for professional training, a lot of activities and other benefits to discover. unil.ch/work Contact for further information For any specific enquiries, please contact: Stéphanie Tissot, Head of SOxHiF : stephanie.tissot@unil.ch Your application Deadline: 26 October 2026 Please submit your application including a CV, a letter of motivation via the UNIL application service. Job description Click here to open the job description. Additional information Niveaux 1 à 12 : UNIL is committed to: •    equality, diversity and inclusion within its community; •    ensuring an open and respectful environment that is conducive to personal development; •    offering working conditions that facilitate work-life balance. unil.ch/equality unil.ch/families Niveaux 13 et + : UNIL is committed to: •    equality, diversity and inclusion 