      "title": "Postdoc research in synthetic immunology",
      "description": "Career Opportunities: Postdoc research in synthetic immunology (22995) JavaScript is turned off in your web browser. Turn it on to take full advantage of this site, then refresh the page. Loading... Skip to Main Content Career Opportunities: Postdoc research in synthetic immunology (22995) Requisition ID 22995 - Posted - Type of position (1) - Area of Activity (1) - Rate of Participation (1) - Faculty / Service (1) - Personnel Category (1)  Job Description Print Preview Apply Save Job Email Job to Friend Return to List Introduction UNIL is a leading international teaching and research institution, with over 5,000 employees and 17,000 students split between its Dorigny campus, CHUV and Epalinges. As an employer, UNIL encourages excellence, individual recognition and responsibility. unil.ch/work Presentation The departement/group Ping-Chih Ho of the University of Lausanne invites applications for the position of Postdoc research in synthetic immunology Job information Expected start date in position : 01/01/2027 Contract length : 1 year, with a possibility to be renewed Employment rate : 100% Workplace : Epalinges Your responsibilities Under the supervision of the group leader, autonomous following of in vivo experiments of immunotherapy of cancer and planning of in vivo experiments testing novel compounds Conducting research activities covering flow cytometry, in vivo experiment, human sample handling and writing reports, including progress report and manuscript. Your qualifications PhD degree in Biotechnology, Biochemistry, Molecular Biology or equivalent Capable to perform animal experiments FACS Training Fluent English speaking ability and excellent communication skill What the position offers you We offer a nice working place in a multicultural, diversified and dynamic academic environment, opportunities for professional training. unil.ch/work Contact for further information Prof Ping-Chih Ho (email pingchihholab@gmail.com) Tél : 0216925947 Your application Application deadline : 01.11.2026 Please include your full application (CV, two reference letters and certificate for module 1 animal training). Only applications through this website will be taken into account. We thank you for your understanding. Additional information UNIL is committed to: •    equality, diversity and inclusion within its community; •    ensuring an open and respectful environment that is conducive to personal development; •    offering working conditions that facilitate work-life balance; •    supporting early career researchers. unil.ch/equality unil.ch/families unil.ch/graduatecampus Apply Save Job Email Job to Friend Return to List Email this job to a friend   The job has been sent to Please provide the information below Job title: * Your friend’s email address: Message: * Confirm you are not a robot: Send Cancel Powered by SuccessFactors"
