    "https://career5.successfactors.eu/career?career_ns=job_listing&company=universitdP&navBarLevel=JOB_SEARCH&rcm_site_locale=en_US&career_job_req_id=22996": {
      "title": "What the position offers you",
      "description": "Career Opportunities: Doctoral Student SNSF in Law/Criminology (22996) JavaScript is turned off in your web browser. Turn it on to take full advantage of this site, then refresh the page. Loading... Skip to Main Content Career Opportunities: Doctoral Student SNSF in Law/Criminology (22996) Requisition ID 22996 - Posted - Type of position (1) - Area of Activity (1) - Rate of Participation (1) - Faculty / Service (1) - Personnel Category (1)  Job Description Print Preview Apply Save Job Email Job to Friend Return to List Introduction UNIL is a leading international teaching and research institution, with over 5,000 employees and 17,000 students split between its Dorigny campus, CHUV and Epalinges. As an employer, UNIL encourages excellence, individual recognition and responsibility. unil.ch/work Presentation The School of Criminal Justice of the Faculty of Law, Criminal Justice and Public Administration opens a position of Doctoral Student SNSF in Law/Criminology mainly funded by a Starting Grant from the Swiss National Science Foundation and co-funded by UNIL. Description of the project You will work on a research project funded by a Starting Grant from the Swiss National Science Foundation (SNSF Starting Grant PS00-1_234763). The project is titled “Crime Control in Fragmented Societies (CONNECT)” and its Principal Investigator is Prof. Clara Rigoni, University of Lausanne. The project examines how cooperation between state authorities and certain ethnic and religious minorities takes place in crime control, and how this cooperation is perceived by the actors involved. The project takes Switzerland as a case study and focuses on state-community cooperation in two main phases: 1) in processes of legislation (criminal law) and policy making; 2) in crime prevention. In particular, the project will analyse pioneering police units (so-called Brückenbauer) and other programs (e.g. institutionalized platforms and dialogues) set up in several Swiss cantons and cities aimed at enhancing trust and cooperation between Swiss authorities and ethnic and religious minorities. CONNECT adopts an interdisciplinary methodology combining legal and policy analysis with qualitative empirical research, including interviews with institutional and community actors and observations of activities involving state authorities and minority communities. Job information Starting date : 01.02.2027 (or by agreement) Contract length : The appointment is structured as follows: 1 + 2 + 1 years (4 years in total). Activity rate : 100% Workplace : University of Lausanne, Lausanne-Dorigny. Fieldwork and travel within Switzerland. Possibility of home office according to UNIL regulations. Job insertion : The position is placed under the responsibility of Clara Rigoni, Assistant Professor, School of Criminal Justice, Faculty of Law, Criminal Justice and Public Administration. Salary :  The salary of SNSF Doctoral Students is set by the UNIL Directorate, within the salary range established by the SNSF for this position. Your responsibilities In your activities, you will: Conduct legal and policy analysis relating to legislation (criminal law) and policy affecting ethnic and religious minorities in Switzerland Contribute to the collection and analysis of empirical data, including interviews with institutional actors and other relevant stakeholders Write and complete a PhD in law/criminology under the supervision of Prof. Clara Rigoni and in the framework of the project CONNECT Interact with experts, practitioners and representatives of Swiss and international institutions, NGOs, and scientific organizations Contribute to academic publications, conferences, workshops and other dissemination activities, in Switzerland and abroad Participate actively in the intellectual and academic life of the research group and the School of Criminal Justice Your qualifications To complete our team, we are looking for someone with the following qualifications: Master’s degree in Law and/or Criminology, or an equivalent degree Experience with legal and policy research Knowledge of the Swiss legal system Ability to work independently while also contributing actively to a collaborative research team Excellent written and spoken English Fluency in French or German (knowledge of French is required within one year) Strong interest in combining legal analysis with empirical and interdisciplinary research Experience with qualitative empirical research methods, particularly interviews, is an asset What the position offers you You will gain experience in working in an interdisciplinary team with both academic and non-academic experts in the field of crime control You will work in a rich and stimulating environment at the School of Criminal Justice of the University of Lausanne You can benefit from the Doctoral Progamme of the School of Criminal Justice of the University of Lausanne You can benefit from the financial support of the SNSF for conference participation, open access publications and international networking You will write your PhD in an international, interdisciplinary and collaborative research environment within one of Switzerland’s leading centres for legal and criminological research We offer a nice working place in a multicultural, diverse and dynamic academic environment. Opportunities for professional training, a lot of activities and other benefits to discover. unil.ch/work Contact for further information Clara Rigoni, clara.rigoni@unil.ch Your application Please submit the following documents through the UNIL application platform: A cover letter highlighting your research interests and motivation for the position A comprehensive CV, including a list of publications (if applicable) Copies of university diplomas and degrees, with transcripts (indicating marks/grades) Copy of your Master’s thesis (if not available, please send another research work realized during your Master). One letter of recommendation or the names of one referee. Only applications through this website will be taken into account. Application deadline : 08.11.2026. Shortlisted candidates will be invited for an interview. Additional information UNIL is committed to: •    equality, diversity and inclusion within its community; •    ensuring an open and respectful environment that is conducive to personal development; •    offering working conditions that facilitate work-life balance; •    supporting early career researchers. unil.ch/equality unil.ch/families unil.ch/graduatecampus Apply Save Job Email Job to Friend Return to List Email this job to a friend   The job has been sent to Please provide the information below Job title: * Your friend’s email address: Message: * Confirm you are not a robot: Send Cancel Powered by SuccessFactors"
    },
    "https://career5.successfactors.eu/career?career_ns=job_listing&company=universitdP&navBarLevel=JOB_SEARCH&rcm_site_locale=en_US&career_job_req_id=22746": {
      "title": "What the position offers you",
      "description": "Career Opportunities: PhD Position SNSF Project\"Beyond the Gig Economy:Exploring the New Frontiers of Algorithmic Control\" (22746) JavaScript is turned off in your web browser. Turn it on to take full advantage of this site, then refresh the page. Loading... Skip to Main Content Career Opportunities: PhD Position SNSF Project\"Beyond the Gig Economy:Exploring the New Frontiers of Algorithmic Control\" (22746) Requisition ID 22746 - Posted - Type of position (1) - Area of Activity (3) - Rate of Participation (1) - Faculty / Service (1) - Personnel Category (1)  Job Description Print Preview Apply Save Job Email Job to Friend Return to List Introduction UNIL is a leading international teaching and research institution, with over 5,000 employees and 17,000 students split between its Dorigny campus, CHUV and Epalinges. As an employer, UNIL encourages excellence, individual recognition and responsibility. unil.ch/work Presentation The Swiss Graduate School of Public Administration (IDHEAP) at the University of Lausanne invites applications for a PhD position in the \"Information Management\" research unit headed by Prof. Tobias Mettler. IDHEAP is the largest university institute in Switzerland dedicated entirely and exclusively to the public sector. We offer excellent research support in a dynamic public policy and public administration research community and are committed to promoting the careers of young scholars. Are you interested in the future of AI and the algorithmic state? Are you enthusiastic about developing research at the crossroads between Public Management and Information Systems? Join our research team in the project “Beyond the Gig Economy: Exploring the New Frontiers of Algorithmic Control”. The project examines the implications and different design alternatives of algorithms gradually replacing human decision-making. A core problem we will explore is how social norms can be encoded into algorithmic control while enabling meaningful exception handling. The ideal candidate is therefore sensitive to technical and social questions and interested in conducting challenging empirical work in a fast-moving environment. Job information Expected start date in position : November 1, 2026 / to be agreed Contract length : 1 year, renewable 2 x, maximum 4 years Activity rate : 100% Workplace : Lausanne, IDHEAP building Your responsibilities Their tasks will involve field research, design research, and publication in the field of Information Systems and related. They will spend between 10% and 20% of their time on administrative tasks. Your qualifications In order to complete our team, we are looking for someone with the following skills : -    Master's degree in information systems, management (with a minor in innovation, technology, or computer science) -    Interest in artificial intelligence beyond prompting -    Good knowledge of qualitative research and sensitive to interdisciplinary work -    Passion for writing and presenting research findings to a variety of audiences -    Ability to work both independently and as part of a team -    Innovative, accurate, reliable and persistent; -    Excellent knowledge of English; Excellent knowledge of French or German. What the position offers you -    Integration in a young, and dynamic research group in a leading institute of public administration with highly motivated and engaged members -    Funding for full time (100%) for four years, subject to approval of the PhD proposal by the end of the first year -    Attractive salary and additional financial support for conferences and methodological courses We offer a nice working place in a multicultural, diverse and dynamic academic environment. Opportunities for professional training, a lot of activities and other benefits to discover. unil.ch/work Contact for further information Further inquiries can be directed to Tobias.Mettler@unil.ch Your application Deadline : October 28, 2026 Please, send your full application (letter of motivation, current CV, transcripts, master's thesis (including a short summary)), and the contact information of two people who are willing to serve as references) in Word or PDF. Only applications through this website will be taken into account. We thank you for your understanding. Additional information UNIL is committed to: •    equality, diversity and inclusion within its community; •    ensuring an open and respectful environment that is conducive to personal development; •    offering working conditions that facilitate work-life balance; •    supporting early career researchers. unil.ch/equality unil.ch/families unil.ch/graduatecampus Apply Save Job Email Job to Friend Return to List Email this job to a friend   The job has been sent to Please provide the information below Job title: * Your friend’s email address: Message: * Confirm you are not a robot: Send Cancel Powered by SuccessFactors"
    },
    "https://career5.successfactors.eu/career?career_ns=job_listing&company=universitdP&navBarLevel=JOB_SEARCH&rcm_site_locale=en_US&career_job_req_id=23009": {
      "title": "Secrétaire aux affaires étudiantes",
      "description": "Career Opportunities: Secrétaire aux affaires étudiantes (23009) JavaScript is turned off in your web browser. Turn it on to take full advantage of this site, then refresh the page. Loading... Skip to Main Content Sign In Language English US ‎(English US)‎ Collapsed. To expand press enter Expanded. To collapse press enter  This job requisition is not posted in the locale you requested. Please select an available locale from the dropdown. No Selection Français ‎(French)‎ Career Opportunities: Secrétaire aux affaires étudiantes (23009) Requisition ID 23009 - Posted 10/26/2026 - Type of position (1) - Area of Activity (1) - Rate of Participation (1) - Faculty / Service (1) - Personnel Category (1)  Job Description Print Preview Apply Save Job Email Job to Friend Return to List Introduction Institution d’enseignement et de recherche de premier plan au niveau international, l’UNIL compte près de 5’000 collaboratrices et collaborateurs et 17’000 étudiant·e·s, réparti·e·s entre le campus de Dorigny et les sites du CHUV et d’Epalinges. En tant qu’employeur, elle encourage l’excellence, la reconnaissance des personnes et la responsabilité. unil.ch/travailler Présentation Dans le cadre du départ à la retraite de notre collègue, le Secrétariat des étudiant·e·s de l'Ecole de droit de la Faculté de droit, des sciences criminelles et d'administration publique est à la recherche d'un·e Secrétaire à 70%. Informations liées au poste Entrée en fonction : 01.03.2027 ou à convenir Durée du contrat : indéterminée Taux d'activité : 70% Lieu de travail : Lausanne Dorigny Vos activités Dans vos activités, vous serez amené·e à : •    Assurer le fonctionnement du secrétariat des étudiant·e·s : accueil des étudiant·e·s et renseignements relatifs à l’organisation des études ; •    Assumer la gestion des examens de niveau Bachelor et Master : de leur planification au suivi des résultats (communication des résultats, grades etc.) ; •    Assurer le traitement administratif des recours des étudiant·e·s, de leur réception à la transmission des dossiers à la Commission de recours, en sollicitant les déterminations des parties concernées ; •    Garantir la compatibilité des horaires des enseignements avec les enseignant·e·s et en informer les étudiant·e·s ; •    Gérer les dossiers des étudiant·e·s depuis leur création jusqu'à l’archivage ; •    Organiser la cérémonie de remise des diplômes. Votre profil Afin de compléter notre équipe, nous sommes à la recherche d'une personne avec le profil suivant : CFC d'employé·e de commerce ou titre jugé équivalent ; Quelques années d'expérience dans un poste similaire ; Maîtrise du français écrit et oral ; Maîtrise des outils bureautiques de base (Word, Excel, File Maker, e-mail, agenda électronique, alimentation des pages web (Jahia) ; Excellentes capacités à travailler en équipe, à partager les tâches et à s'adapter à l'évolution des besoins et des outils ; Efficacité dans l'organisation, respect des procédures, sens de la représentation ; Capactié d'adaptation en fonction des différent·e·s interlocuteurs/trices ; Flexibilité dans les horaires (présence accrue nécessaire lors des sessions d'examens). Vos avantages Un cadre de travail agréable dans un environnement académique multiculturel et diversifié. Des possibilités de formation continue, une multitude d'activités et d'autres avantages à découvrir. Davantage d'informations sur unil.ch/travailler Pour tout renseignement complémentaire Livia Danieli ou Mahdiya Cadot, adjointes +41216922761 adjointes.droit@unil.ch Votre dossier de candidature Délai de postulation : 10.11.2026 Nous vous invitons à nous transmettre votre dossier complet en format Word ou PDF. Il ne sera pris en compte que les candidatures adressées par le biais de ce site. Nous vous remercions de votre compréhension. Cahier des charges du poste Cliquez ici pour afficher le cahier des charges. Remarques L’UNIL s’engage : •    Pour l’égalité, la diversité et l’inclusion au sein de sa communauté ; •    À garantir un environnement ouvert, respectueux et propice à l’épanouissement ; •    À offrir des conditions de travail favorables à la conciliation des différentes sphères de vie. unil.ch/egalite unil.ch/familles Apply Save Job Email Job to Friend Return to List Email this job to a friend   The job has been sent to Please provide the information below Job title: * Your friend’s email address: Message: * Confirm you are not a robot: Send Cancel Powered by SuccessFactors"
    },
    "https://career5.successfactors.eu/career?career_ns=job_listing&company=universitdP&navBarLevel=JOB_SEARCH&rcm_site_locale=en_US&career_job_req_id=23013": {
      "title": "Chercheur·euse FNS junior (50%) en sciences sociales ou humanités numériques",
      "description": "Career Opportunities: Chercheur·euse FNS junior (50%) en sciences sociales ou humanités numériques (23013) JavaScript is turned off in your web browser. Turn it on to take full advantage of this site, then refresh the page. Loading... Skip to Main Content Sign In Language English US ‎(English US)‎ Collapsed. To expand press enter Expanded. To collapse press enter  This job requisition is not posted in the locale you requested. Please select an available locale from the dropdown. No Selection Français ‎(French)‎ Career Opportunities: Chercheur·euse FNS junior (50%) en sciences sociales ou humanités numériques (23013) Requisition ID 23013 - Posted 10/26/2026 - Type of position (1) - Area of Activity (1) - Rate of Participation (1) - Faculty / Service (1) - Personnel Category (1)  Job Description Print Preview Apply Save Job Email Job to Friend Return to List Introduction Institution d’enseignement et de recherche de premier plan au niveau international, l’UNIL compte près de 5’000 collaboratrices et collaborateurs et 17’000 étudiant·e·s, réparti·e·s entre le campus de Dorigny et les sites du CHUV et d’Epalinges. En tant qu’employeur, elle encourage l’excellence, la reconnaissance des personnes et la responsabilité. unil.ch/travailler Présentation Dans le cadre d’un projet de recherche international financé par le Fonds National Suisse de la Recherche scientifique (FNS) intitulé : « Performing Artificial Intelligence: Governance, Agency, Action – An Interdisciplinary Inquiry », l'Institut des sciences sociales (ISS) de l’Université de Lausanne, met au concours un poste de : Chercheuse/chercheur FNS junior (50%) en sciences sociales ou humanités numériques Objectifs du projet/Description du projet Le projet « Performing Artificial Intelligence » (PAI) vise à comprendre l’intelligence artificielle comme un objet social et culturel dynamique, qui se construit par le discours et la pratique dans des contextes spécifiques. Informations liées au poste Entrée en fonction :      1er janvier 2027 Durée du contrat :        1 an, contrat renouvelable pour 1 ans, maximum 2 ans Taux d'activité :            50% Lieu de travail :            Université de Lausanne, Géopolis Salaire : Selon barême FNS et années d’expérience Vos activités Pour approfondir l’analyse de la compréhension, du développement et de la critique de nouveaux systèmes d’IA, nous mettons au concours un Poste de chercheuse/chercheur FNS junior (50%). Nous cherchons une personne intéressée à s’engager dans l’ethnographie d’usages quotidiens de systèmes d’IA et, plus particulièrement, sur deux corpus de données pertinentes du projet : Premièrement, un corpus existant composé d’enregistrements audiovisuels d’interactions filmées avec ce type de systèmes et des systèmes robotiques dans des situations quotidiennes, d’une part, et d’un premier sondage mené au sujet des usages sociaux de nouveaux systèmes d’IA, de l’autre ; Deuxièmement, un nouveau corpus de données empiriques en train d’être constitué à partir d’enregistrements audiovisuels et de notes ethnographiques issus de situations de recherche impliquant des experts en matière d’art numérique, d’IA et/ou de robotique. La personne intéressée contribuera à l’expérimentation avec des technologies numériques en situation et à l’ethnographie et à l’analyse vidéo de cette expérimentation dans une perspective interdisciplinaire. Voir le cahier des charges détaillé Votre profil BA ou MA en informatique, ingénierie, sociologie, linguistique, anthropologie, études genre, études des médias et/ou dans un domaine apparenté ; Expérience ou intérêt l’expérimentation avec des technologies numériques en situation (via des « hacks » et des « prompts ») et l’ethnographie de cette expérimentation et, plus généralement, les études sociales des sciences et des techniques en action ; Disponibilité à s’engager dans et à analyser l’expérimentation avec des technologies numériques en situation, au moyen de descriptions détaillées et d’analyses vidéo, intérêt pour la philosophie de l’esprit et de l’intelligence artificielle, ouverture au dialogue interdisciplinaire ; Disponibilité au travail de terrain, hors site, en Suisse et/ou à l’étranger ; Expérience ou intérêt pour le dépouillement, l’analyse et la présentation de résultats de sondage mené au sujet d’usages sociaux ou de pratiques sociales ; Maîtrise du français et de l’anglais, à l’oral et à l’écrit. L’allemand serait un atout. Vos avantages Un cadre de travail agréable dans un environnement académique multiculturel et diversifié. Des possibilités de formation continue, d’échanges scientifiques de haut niveau et de consolidation d’un profil académique en devenir. Davantage d'informations sur unil.ch/travailler Pour tout renseignement complémentaire Monsieur Olivier Glassey Maître d'enseignement et de recherche olivier.glassey@unil.ch Votre dossier de candidature Veuillez joindre à votre dossier de candidature : (1) Une lettre de motivation (2) Un CV académique avec le nom de deux personnes de références (3)Un texte académique (chapitre de mémoire, travail de séminaire, article scientifique, etc.) Il ne sera pris en compte que les candidatures adressées par le biais de ce site. Merci d’adresser votre dossier complet en format Word ou PDF. Délai de candidature : 8 novembre 2026 Les entretiens auront probablement lieu entre le 23 et 24 novembre 2026. Remarques L’UNIL s’engage : •    Pour l’égalité, la diversité et l’inclusion au sein de sa communauté ; •    À garantir un environnement ouvert, respectueux et propice à l’épanouissement ; •    À offrir des conditions de travail favorables à la conciliation des différentes sphères de vie ; •    À soutenir la relève scientifique. unil.ch/egalite unil.ch/familles unil.ch/graduatecampus Apply Save Job Email Job to Friend Return to List Email this job to a friend   The job has been sent to Please provide the information below Job title: * Your friend’s email address: Message: * Confirm you are not a robot: Send Cancel Powered by SuccessFactors"
    },
    "https://career5.successfactors.eu/career?career_ns=job_listing&company=universitdP&navBarLevel=JOB_SEARCH&rcm_site_locale=en_US&career_job_req_id=23014": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Researcher in Next-Generation T-Cell Engineering",
      "description": "Career Opportunities: Postdoctoral Researcher in Next-Generation T-Cell Engineering (23014) JavaScript is turned off in your web browser. Turn it on to take full advantage of this site, then refresh the page. Loading... Skip to Main Content Career Opportunities: Postdoctoral Researcher in Next-Generation T-Cell Engineering (23014) Requisition ID 23014 - Posted - Type of position (1) - Area of Activity (1) - Rate of Participation (1) - Faculty / Service (1) - Personnel Category (1)  Job Description Print Preview Apply Save Job Email Job to Friend Return to List Introduction UNIL is a leading international teaching and research institution, with over 5,000 employees and 17,000 students split between its Dorigny campus, CHUV and Epalinges. As an employer, UNIL encourages excellence, individual recognition and responsibility. unil.ch/work Presentation The T-cell Engineering Laboratory led by Dr Melita Irving in the Department of Fundamental Oncology at the University of Lausanne invites applications for a Postdoctoral Researcher in Next-Generation T-Cell Engineering. Our team develops innovative CAR- and TCR-engineered T-cell therapies for cancer, combining cellular immunology, genetic engineering and preclinical research. We welcome candidates with strong immunology expertise, including complementary research backgrounds, who are enthusiastic about advancing cancer immunotherapy. Job information Expected start date in position : 01.12.2026 Contract length : 1 year Employment rate : 100% Workplace : Epalinges, Lausanne Your responsibilities Develop and characterise next-generation CAR- and TCR-engineered T cells, using molecular and cellular immunology approaches. Design and perform in vitro experiments, including multiparameter flow cytometry, cytokine production and cytotoxicity assays, using T-cell/tumour-cell cocultures, tumour spheroids and patient-derived tumour material. Participate in and perform in vivo preclinical tumour studies, following completion of the required training and authorisations. Independently lead a defined research project, including experimental planning, documentation, data analysis, troubleshooting and communication of results, while contributing to manuscripts and collaborating closely with laboratory members and external collaborators. Contribute to general laboratory maintenance, organisation and shared responsibilities, as coordinated by the laboratory manager. Work in a cordial, respectful, diligent and rigorous manner. Your qualifications PhD in immunology or a related biomedical discipline; applicants with complementary immunology backgrounds are encouraged. Strong practical immunology skills, including cell culture, flow cytometry, molecular biology and/or functional immune assays. Experience in T-cell culture, genetic modification or CAR/TCR engineering is advantageous. Willingness to undertake in vivo experimental studies is essential. Previous experience with animal models and LTK1 certification are advantageous but not required. The successful candidate will be expected to complete the necessary training and obtain the relevant authorisations. Scientific curiosity, rigour, independence, teamwork and strong written and spoken English. What the position offers you Join a dynamic, international and collaborative research team dedicated to developing innovative T-cell therapies for cancer. We offer a stimulating scientific environment with opportunities to contribute to cutting-edge research in CAR and TCR engineering, develop expertise in advanced in vitro and in vivo preclinical models, and work alongside researchers with complementary expertise. The position provides opportunities for scientific independence, professional development and collaboration within a supportive academic environment. Contact for further information Dr Melita Irving (email: Melita.Irving@unil.ch) Tél : +41216925961 Your application Application deadline : 09.10.2026 Please include a motivation letter, full curriculum vitae with publication list, and contact details for two referees. Only applications through this website will be taken into account. We thank you for your understanding. Additional information UNIL is committed to: •    equality, diversity and inclusion within its community; •    ensuring an open and respectful environment that is conducive to personal development; •    offering working conditions that facilitate work-life balance; •    supporting early career researchers. unil.ch/equality unil.ch/families unil.ch/graduatecampus Apply Save Job Email Job to Friend Return to List Email this job to a friend   The job has been sent to Please provide the information below Job title: * Your friend’s email address: Message: * Confirm you are not a robot: Send Cancel Powered by SuccessFactors"
    },
    "https://career5.successfactors.eu/career?career_ns=job_listing&company=universitdP&navBarLevel=JOB_SEARCH&rcm_site_locale=en_US&career_job_req_id=23011": {
      "title": "Graduate Assistant in Actuarial Science",
      "description": "Career Opportunities: Graduate Assistant in Actuarial Science (23011) JavaScript is turned off in your web browser. Turn it on to take full advantage of this site, then refresh the page. Loading... Skip to Main Content Career Opportunities: Graduate Assistant in Actuarial Science (23011) Requisition ID 23011 - Posted - Type of position (1) - Area of Activity (1) - Rate of Participation (1) - Faculty / Service (1) - Personnel Category (1)  Job Description Print Preview Apply Save Job Email Job to Friend Return to List Introduction UNIL is a leading international teaching and research institution, with over 5,000 employees and 17,000 students split between its Dorigny campus, CHUV and Epalinges. As an employer, UNIL encourages excellence, individual recognition and responsibility. unil.ch/work Presentation The Department of Actuarial Science of the Faculty of Business and Economics (HEC) is looking for two Graduate Assistants in Actuarial Science Job information Expected start date in position : September 1, 2027 or to be agreed Contract length : 1 year, renewable 2 x 2 years, maximum 5 years Activity rate : 80 % Workplace : Lausanne Dorigny, Extranef building Salary: Pay scales Supervisor: Prof. Enkelejd Hashorva Your responsibilities 50% of the time will be dedicated to completion of doctoral studies in actuarial science. 50% of the assistant's time will be dedicated to teaching, administrative (including exam supervision), technical and research support for the department. Your qualifications Master of Science (MSc) in Actuarial Science or equivalent. Strong desire to write a theoretical thesis in actuarial science based on extreme value theory or random processes. Fluent in English, French an asset Ability to work in a team and good communication skills. What the position offers you We offer a nice working place in a multicultural, diverse and dynamic academic environment. Opportunities for professional training, a lot of activities and other benefits to discover. unil.ch/work Contact for further information Please contact the Department of Actuarial Science (DSA): catherine.lombardvonlanthen[at]unil.ch Your application Only applications through this website will be taken into account. The application file may be in Word or PDF format, but cannot be compressed. Letter of motivation and CV with references. Copies of university diplomas and degrees; transcripts (indicating marks/grades achieved). An example of a research project, if available (e.g. master thesis, seminar work, etc) Application deadline: March 31, 2027 Additional information UNIL is committed to: •    equality, diversity and inclusion within its community; •    ensuring an open and respectful environment that is conducive to personal development; •    offering working conditions that facilitate work-life balance; •    supporting early career researchers. unil.ch/equality unil.ch/families unil.ch/graduatecampus Apply Save Job Email Job to Friend Return to List Email this job to a friend   The job has been sent to Please provide the information below Job title: * Your friend’s email address: Message: * Confirm you are not a robot: Send Cancel Powered by SuccessFactors"
