    "https://career5.successfactors.eu/career?career_ns=job_listing&company=universitdP&navBarLevel=JOB_SEARCH&rcm_site_locale=en_US&career_job_req_id=23012": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Researcher in Plant Molecular Biology",
      "description": "Career Opportunities: Postdoctoral Researcher in Plant Molecular Biology (23012) JavaScript is turned off in your web browser. Turn it on to take full advantage of this site, then refresh the page. Loading... Skip to Main Content Career Opportunities: Postdoctoral Researcher in Plant Molecular Biology (23012) Requisition ID 23012 - Posted - Type of position (1) - Area of Activity (1) - Rate of Participation (1) - Faculty / Service (1) - Personnel Category (1)  Job Description Print Preview Apply Save Job Email Job to Friend Return to List Introduction UNIL is a leading international teaching and research institution, with over 5,000 employees and 17,000 students split between its Dorigny campus, CHUV and Epalinges. As an employer, UNIL encourages excellence, individual recognition and responsibility. unil.ch/work Presentation Prof. Christian Hardtke is looking for a Postdoctoral researcher to join his research group at the Department of Plant Molecular Biology (DBMV) at the University of Lausanne. Project Description The candidate will join a project that revolves around organ formation in the model system Brachypodium distachyon, with a focus on molecular mechanisms of peptide signaling pathways. Our lab is located at the University of Lausanne at the Dorigny Campus, by the lake Geneva, in Lausanne. This position is mostly research oriented. It is also associated to teaching duties of undergraduate B.Sc. and M.Sc. students. Your qualifications Candidates who have recently obtained a Ph.D. degree in the Molecular Plant Sciences and ideally worked with grasses or crop systems, and who have a keen interest in plant signaling mechanisms and in learning new methods and skills are encouraged to apply. Job information Expected starting date: 01.01.2027 Contract length: 1 year, option to renew. Activity: 100% Workplace: Lausanne-Dorigny campus What the position offers you An international and interdisciplinary academic working environment with possibilities of continuous training in different techniques. Contact for further information Prof. Christian Hardtke: christian.hardtke@unil.ch Your application Deadline : 15.11.2026 Please, send your full application in Word or PDF. Only applications through this website will be taken into account. We thank you for your understanding. Additional information UNIL is committed to: •    equality, diversity and inclusion within its community; •    ensuring an open and respectful environment that is conducive to personal development; •    offering working conditions that facilitate work-life balance; •    supporting early career researchers. unil.ch/equality unil.ch/families unil.ch/graduatecampus Apply Save Job Email Job to Friend Return to List Email this job to a friend   The job has been sent to Please provide the information below Job title: * Your friend’s email address: Message: * Confirm you are not a robot: Send Cancel Powered by SuccessFactors"
    },
    "https://career5.successfactors.eu/career?career_ns=job_listing&company=universitdP&navBarLevel=JOB_SEARCH&rcm_site_locale=en_US&career_job_req_id=23010": {
      "title": "What the position offers you",
      "description": "Career Opportunities: Postdoctoral position in nuclear lipid signalling and insulin resistance in skeletal muscle (23010) JavaScript is turned off in your web browser. Turn it on to take full advantage of this site, then refresh the page. Loading... Skip to Main Content Career Opportunities: Postdoctoral position in nuclear lipid signalling and insulin resistance in skeletal muscle (23010) Requisition ID 23010 - Posted - Type of position (1) - Area of Activity (1) - Rate of Participation (1) - Faculty / Service (1) - Personnel Category (1)  Job Description Print Preview Apply Save Job Email Job to Friend Return to List Introduction UNIL is a leading international teaching and research institution, with over 5,000 employees and 17,000 students split between its Dorigny campus, CHUV and Epalinges. As an employer, UNIL encourages excellence, individual recognition and responsibility. unil.ch/work Presentation We are seeking a Postdoctoral Researcher to lead a project testing whether defined nuclear diacylglycerol (DAG) species causally regulate insulin action in human skeletal muscle. The project combines tagged-anchored photocaged DAGs, released by light at the nuclear envelope of primary human myotubes, with time-resolved functional, transcriptomic and mitochondrial readouts. These cellular findings will be integrated with organelle-resolved DAG lipidomics and RNA-seq in paired skeletal muscle biopsies collected before and after intervention in a study with volunteers. The position is based in the Aging and Muscle Metabolism laboratory led by Prof. Francesca Amati (Department of Biomedical Sciences, UNIL) and involves close collaboration with partner laboratories specialised in photocaged-lipid chemistry (EPFL, Switzerland) and DAG lipidomics (University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus, USA). Job information Expected start date in position : January 2027 Contract length : 1 year, renewable if funding available Activity rate : 100% Workplace : Département des Sciences biomédicales, Université de Lausanne, Rue du Bugnon 7, CH-1005 Lausanne Your responsibilities The postdoctoral researcher will design, conduct and coordinate the project, from tool validation in human muscle cells to integration with human data. Specifically, they will: •      Establish nuclear-envelope Tag anchors in primary human myoblasts by transfection and validate the localisation and light-controlled release of matched sn-1,2 and 1,3 photocaged DAG probes using confocal imaging, DAG biosensors and fraction-resolved lipidomics. •      Quantify insulin-stimulated glycogen synthesis using radiolabelled glucose and insulin signalling after nuclear DAG release, followed by bulk RNA-seq and Seahorse respirometry. •      Perform subcellular fractionation, targeted DAG lipidomics and bulk RNA-seq on paired pre- and post-intervention skeletal muscle biopsies, and integrate these data with glucose-clamp, metabolic-flexibility and body-composition phenotypes using mixed-effects models. •      Analyse transcriptomic and imaging data with reproducible, version-controlled workflows and apply FAIR data-management practices. •      Coordinate the scientific exchanges with the collaborating chemistry and lipidomics laboratories, co-supervise students, and contribute to teaching in the laboratory. •      Disseminate the results through first-author publications, international conferences and public-engagement activities in French and English, and prepare independent funding applications. Your qualifications The candidate must hold a PhD in biology, physiology or biomedical sciences, obtained within the last five years, with a doctoral thesis, with a strong experience on the regulation of skeletal muscle metabolism by bioactive lipids, preferably sphingolipids/ceramides or diacylglycerols. A dual academic background combining a degree in biotechnology or bioengineering and a degree in sport or exercise sciences is required. Required expertise : •      A track record of first-author publications on lipid-induced insulin resistance and skeletal muscle metabolism, including methodological publications. •      Hands-on expertise in primary human skeletal muscle cell culture (myoblasts and myotubes), cell transfection, and radiolabelled metabolic flux assays (glycogen synthesis, glucose uptake and oxidation, fatty-acid oxidation). •      Experience in both animal and human research: in vivo mouse models of metabolic disease (glucose and insulin tolerance tests, body composition, ex vivo insulin sensitivity) and participation in human clinical studies of physical activity or inactivity combining clinical phenotyping with ex vivo skeletal muscle analyses. •      Knowledge of lipid species diversity and subcellular lipid localisation, and experience in interpreting lipidomic data in the context of insulin resistance. •      Bulk RNA-seq analysis and advanced coding in R and Python, including the development of deep-learning pipelines for microscopy image segmentation and quantitative phenotyping of muscle cells, released as open-source code. •      Widefield and confocal fluorescence microscopy and quantitative image analysis. •      Competitive research funding obtained as principal investigator, in addition to doctoral or postdoctoral fellowships. •      Teaching experience in exercise physiology and cell biology at BSc and MSc levels, and co-supervision of MSc or engineering students. •      Fluency in French and English, with the ability to write scientific texts and communicate with lay audiences in both languages. Personal qualities : The ideal candidate is independent, rigorous and well organised, able to coordinate international collaborations, and motivated to develop an independent research line on compartment-specific lipid signalling in a collaborative laboratory environment. What the position offers you We offer a nice working place in a multicultural, diverse and dynamic academic environment. Opportunities for professional training, a lot of activities and other benefits to discover. unil.ch/work Contact for further information Prof. Francesca Amati Département de Sciences biomédicales, Université de Lausanne Rue du Bugnon 7 CH-1005 Lausanne Your application Deadline : 02.11.2026 Applications are invited in the form of a motivation letter, a curriculum vitae, a brief description of research experience and doctoral thesis, and the names and addresses of three academic references, before November, 2026. Applications must also include a research statement (maximum two pages) describing how the candidate would establish a causal link between specific nuclear diacylglycerol species and insulin action in primary human myotubes using photocaged lipids, and how they would integrate these findings with lipidomic and transcriptomic data from paired human skeletal muscle biopsies. Applications without this statement will not be considered.  Please, send your full application in Word or PDF. Only applications through this website will be taken into account. We thank you for your understanding. Additional information UNIL is committed to: •    equality, diversity and inclusion within its community; •    ensuring an open and respectful environment that is conducive to personal development; •    offering working conditions that facilitate work-life balance; •    supporting early career researchers. unil.ch/equality unil.ch/families unil.ch/graduatecampus Apply Save Job Email Job to Friend Return to List Email this job to a friend   The job has been sent to Please provide the information below Job title: * Your friend’s email address: Message: * Confirm you are not a robot: Send Cancel Powered by SuccessFactors"
    },
    "https://career5.successfactors.eu/career?career_ns=job_listing&company=universitdP&navBarLevel=JOB_SEARCH&rcm_site_locale=en_US&career_job_req_id=23007": {
      "title": "What the position offers you",
      "description": "Career Opportunities: Knowledge and Technology Transfer (KTT) Manager - NCCR Genesis (23007) JavaScript is turned off in your web browser. Turn it on to take full advantage of this site, then refresh the page. Loading... Skip to Main Content Career Opportunities: Knowledge and Technology Transfer (KTT) Manager - NCCR Genesis (23007) Requisition ID 23007 - Posted - Type of position (1) - Area of Activity (1) - Rate of Participation (1) - Faculty / Service (1) - Personnel Category (1)  Job Description Print Preview Apply Save Job Email Job to Friend Return to List Introduction UNIL is a leading international teaching and research institution, with over 5,000 employees and 17,000 students split between its Dorigny campus, CHUV and Epalinges. As an employer, UNIL encourages excellence, individual recognition and responsibility. unil.ch/work About NCCR Genesis The National Centre of Competence in Research (NCCR) Genesis is a Swiss research network bringing together leading scientists from multiple institutions to advance interdisciplinary research across physics, chemistry, Earth sciences and related disciplines. Alongside its scientific activities, NCCR Genesis promotes innovation, knowledge and technology transfer, entrepreneurship, and collaboration with industry. Details on NCCR Genesis are available on its website https://nccr-genesis.ch . NCCR Genesis is deeply committed to equality, diversity and inclusion. Our aim is to cultivate a respectful and fair work culture with equal access to professional development and support for all. We strongly encourage applications from under-represented groups. Presentation We are seeking a Knowledge and Technology Transfer (KTT) Manager to strengthen connections between NCCR Genesis researchers and the private sector, identify opportunities for innovation and commercialisation, and facilitate industrial partnerships. Working closely with the NCCR management, research teams and technology transfer offices of partner institutions, you will contribute to translating scientific discoveries into practical applications and societal and economic impact. Job information Expected start date in position : 01.01.2027 / to be agreed Contract length : 4 years (2+2) Activity rate :  50 to 60 % Workplace : UNIL -Géopolis - Earth Sciences Institute - NCCR GENESIS Team Your responsibilities Technology scouting and valorisation: identify promising research results, assess their potential for industrial applications, and facilitate technology transfer, intellectual property protection, licensing and spin-off initiatives in collaboration with institutional specialists. Industrial partnerships: Identify and engage industrial partners, develop strategic relationships and facilitate collaborative research and innovation projects. Innovation and entrepreneurship: Support researchers in accessing entrepreneurship programmes, innovation funding and commercialisation opportunities within the Swiss innovation ecosystem. Knowledge exchange and talent development: Promote interactions between academia and industry, develop private-sector internship opportunities for early-career researchers, and coordinate networking activities, including the annual Genesis Tech Days. KTT coordination: Contribute to the implementation and monitoring of knowledge transfer activities in collaboration with partner institutions. Your qualifications In order to complete our team, we are looking for someone with the following skills : Master’s or PhD in physics, chemistry, Earth sciences, or another discipline relevant to NCCR Genesis. At least three years of relevant professional experience in industry, technology transfer, innovation management or industrial partnerships. Demonstrated ability to identify innovation opportunities and develop relationships with industrial stakeholders. Understanding of technology commercialisation, intellectual property and entrepreneurship. Excellent communication, networking and interpersonal skills, combined with a proactive, independent and results-oriented approach. Excellent command of English; knowledge of French and German is required. Familiarity with the Swiss innovation ecosystem and its funding instruments is an advantage. What the position offers you An opportunity to work at the interface of cutting-edge interdisciplinary research, innovation and industry within a collaborative Swiss research network. You will interact with leading researchers, technology transfer professionals and industrial partners, contributing directly to the impact of NCCR Genesis research. We offer a nice working place in a multicultural, diverse and dynamic academic environment. Opportunities for professional training, a lot of activities and other benefits to discover. unil.ch/work Contact for further information Prof. Johanna MARIN CARBONNE  UNIL / ISTE : johanna.marincarbonne@unil.ch Prof. Nicolas Winssinger UNIGE : Nicolas.Winssinger@unige.ch Alberto Schena : alberto.schena@unil.ch Your application Deadline : 22/11/2026 Please, send your full application in Word or PDF. Only applications through this website will be taken into account. We thank you for your understanding. Job description Click here to open the job description. Additional information UNIL is committed to: •    equality, diversity and inclusion within its community; •    ensuring an open and respectful environment that is conducive to personal development; •    offering working conditions that facilitate work-life balance. unil.ch/equality unil.ch/families Apply Save Job Email Job to Friend Return to List Email this job to a friend   The job has been sent to Please provide the information below Job title: * Your friend’s email address: Message: * Confirm you are not a robot: Send Cancel Powered by SuccessFactors"
    },
    "https://career5.successfactors.eu/career?career_ns=job_listing&company=universitdP&navBarLevel=JOB_SEARCH&rcm_site_locale=en_US&career_job_req_id=23005": {
      "title": "Assistant·e diplômé·e en Biochimie de l'Exercice",
      "description": "Career Opportunities: Assistant·e diplômé·e en Biochimie de l'Exercice (23005) JavaScript is turned off in your web browser. Turn it on to take full advantage of this site, then refresh the page. Loading... Skip to Main Content Career Opportunities: Assistant·e diplômé·e en Biochimie de l'Exercice (23005) Requisition ID 23005 - Posted - Type of position (1) - Area of Activity (1) - Rate of Participation (1) - Faculty / Service (1) - Personnel Category (1)  Job Description Print Preview Apply Save Job Email Job to Friend Return to List Introduction Institution d’enseignement et de recherche de premier plan au niveau international, l’UNIL compte près de 5’000 collaboratrices et collaborateurs et 17’000 étudiant·e·s, réparti·e·s entre le campus de Dorigny et les sites du CHUV et d’Epalinges. En tant qu’employeur, elle encourage l’excellence, la reconnaissance des personnes et la responsabilité. unil.ch/travailler Présentation L'Institut des Sciences du Sport (ISSUL) de l’Université de Lausanne met au concours un poste de Assistant·e diplômé·e en Biochimie de l’Exercice Informations liées au poste Entrée en fonction : 01.02.2027 Durée du contrat : 1 an, renouvelable 2 x 2 ans, maximum 5 ans Taux d'activité : 100% Lieu de travail : Lausanne Salaire annuel brut : CHF 67'568, en progression chaque année selon le barème Vos activités Le poste est placé sous la responsabilité de Nadège Zanou. Il est attendu du ou de la titulaire qu’il ou elle développe des travaux de recherche innovants et de niveau international dans le domaine de la biochimie de l'exercice à l'ISSUL. Les travaux porteront principalement sur les mécanismes moléculaires d’adaptation du muscle squelettique à l'exercice, notamment ceux qui régissent la manière dont l'exercice, en fonction de ses modalités, modifie l'accessibilité du génome et l'expression des protéines en lien avec le métabolisme musculaire. 50% du taux d'activité sera dédié à la réalisation d'une thèse de doctorat. 25% du taux d'activité sera consacré au soutien des tâches d'enseignement. 25% du taux d'activité sera consacré aux travaux de recherche partagés. Voir le cahier des charges Votre profil Nous souhaitons engager une personne avec le profil suivant : Vous avez un Master en en sciences du sport, biologie, sciences biomédicales, médecine, pharmacie ou titre jugé équivalent. Vous avez un intérêt à poursuivre des activités de recherche et d’élaborer une thèse dans le domaine de de la biochimie de l’exercice, en lien avec les intérêts de recherche du groupe de Nadège Zanou ( ISSUL-FBM). Vous avez la maîtrise du français et bonnes connaissances de l’anglais. Vous avez un intérêt pour l’enseignement de la physiologie et biochimie de l’exercice ainsi ou l’activité physique appliquée à la santé. Vous justifiez d'une expérience dans les domaines suivants : physiologie de l’effort chez l’humain ou la souris, mesures de la force musculaire et cultures de cellules musculaires, qPCR, Western blot, imagerie calcique, Oroboros O2k et/ou ATaq-seq, édition génétique, profilage ribosomique, biologie computationnelle ou analyse de données OMICs. Vous disposez d’une certification vous permettant de travailler avec des modèles animaux en Suisse (un atout). Vous avez un sens de l’organisation, capacité à travailler de façon autonome et indépendante, et au sein d’une équipe de recherche. La préférence sera donnée à une personne ouverte à la communication et à la coopération, et capable de travailler en équipe. Vos avantages Un cadre de travail agréable dans un environnement académique multiculturel et diversifié. Des possibilités de formation continue, une multitude d'activités et d'autres avantages à découvrir. Un soutien organisationnel permettant de participer à des colloques internationaux et la tenue d’événements scientifiques. Davantage d'informations sur unil.ch/travailler Pour tout renseignement complémentaire Veuillez contacter Nadège Zanou Adresse mail : nadege.zanou@unil.ch Votre dossier de candidature Délai de candidature : 04.11.2026 Nous vous prions de bien vouloir nous transmettre les documents ci-dessous en un dossier unique en format PDF via la plateforme de recrutement : Lettre de motivation, CV académique avec copie des diplômes universitaires et relevés des notes obtenues, Un bref exposé (1 page maximum) de vos travaux de recherche antérieurs. Un résumé (1 page maximum) de votre expérience pédagogique antérieure (le cas échéant). Le nom et le contact de votre superviseur de Master Une copie de vos diplômes Une carte d’identité valide Seules les candidatures adressées par le biais de ce site seront prises en compte. Remarque : les entretiens avec les candidats présélectionnés auront lieu les 17 ou 18 Novembre , soit en présentiel, soit en ligne via Teams. Remarques L’UNIL s’engage : •    Pour l’égalité, la diversité et l’inclusion au sein de sa communauté ; •    À garantir un environnement ouvert, respectueux et propice à l’épanouissement ; •    À offrir des conditions de travail favorables à la conciliation des différentes sphères de vie ; •    À soutenir la relève scientifique. unil.ch/egalite unil.ch/familles unil.ch/graduatecampus Apply Save Job Email Job to Friend Return to List Email this job to a friend   The job has been sent to Please provide the information below Job title: * Your friend’s email address: Message: * Confirm you are not a robot: Send Cancel Powered by SuccessFactors"
